# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/

# Node / frontend
node_modules/
src/frontend/dist/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Downloaded market data — large, and re-fetchable from yfinance on demand.
# Together ~300 MB, changing every trading day; versioning it would bloat the
# history for data the app rebuilds automatically.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
src/backend/app/data/prices/
src/backend/app/data/backtest/prices/

# Vendor caches — rebuilt on demand from NSE / Yahoo.
src/backend/app/data/universes/
src/backend/app/data/fundamentals_cache.json
src/backend/app/data/surveillance_cache.json

# Backtest run OUTPUTS: one ~500 KB JSON of curves, weeks and every trade.
# The run RECORD (config + headline metrics) under runs/ is KEPT — that is the
# research log and it is small. Results regenerate by re-running the config.
src/backend/app/data/backtest/results/

# Working cycle state — regenerated by the app, not source. The durable journal
# (journal.jsonl / journal.md) is deliberately NOT ignored: per the Rulebook it
# is the permanent record, and deleting a cycle must not take it with it.
src/backend/app/data/cycles/
src/backend/app/data/_current_cycle.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PERSONAL FINANCIAL RECORDS — currently TRACKED, on purpose: the ledger and
# journal are irreplaceable, and losing them is worse than versioning them.
#
# Uncomment these BEFORE pushing this repo anywhere public or shared. They
# contain real positions, quantities, entry prices and trade history.
#
# src/backend/app/data/holdings_ledger.csv
# src/backend/app/data/journal.jsonl
# src/backend/app/data/journal.md
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Atomic-write temp files (repositories write .tmp, then os.replace)
*.tmp

# Secrets / local overrides
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Editors & OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
